Z||000000||FieroGT||10-06-1999||11:05 AM||||Some eBay auctions really get me burned up! Currently, there is someone selling a pair of new Fiero ashtrays. The catch is that this is the second auction for the item. The last pair sold for over $21 and this one starts at $10. Don't people know that these things are available at their friendly GM dealer for about $2.50 a piece??? It really gets on my nerves to see people trying to make a killing on parts that enthusiasts such as ourselves need for our cars. Seems that when you say "Fiero" when you're looking for a part at a junkyard, the people assume that it's big bucks. <P>Sorry to vent like this. I guess it's a bad day today. Hopefully it will get better when I get outside and fire up the Fiero. <p>[This message has been edited by FieroGT (edited 10-06-1999).]||||reg||8
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||10-06-1999||01:10 PM||||That's typically eBay for ya. People get so involved in the bidding, they usually end up with a second-hand item that has cost them more than a new one. Seen it happen quite a few times there.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||10-06-1999||04:52 PM||||Once I paid $25 for a "limited edition" poster, the teaser poster for Star Wars: Episode 1.. the day before it arrived in the mail I went to wal-mart and saw the exact same poster for $5....<P>limited edition means a few million posters I guess, I see them everywhere now.. so I now have 2 identical posters, one was printed in canada and one was from the USA.. but they're the same.<P>Not Fiero related obviously, but just another eBay story. I did see someone trying to sell a pair of Fiero seats on a newsgroup for like $250 tho..||||reg||1
Z||000003||Racer 1||10-06-1999||05:44 PM||||I like E-Bay you just got ot know what to look for as far as deals. I got my 86 fiero manaul for 8.00$ was bidding on a factory repair manaul also.||||reg||14
Z||000004||DJRice||10-07-1999||10:46 AM||||I picked up 6 loose fieros for $6.00 on ebay.<BR>3 Matchbox, 2 Hot Wheels, and one Majorette.<BR>These werent in the package, and had been played with but I cleaned them up and they look pretty good.  <P>Of course, I have paid $6.00 each for two still in the package that are several years old.  I did not think that was out of line either.  <P>I did see a laptop on the aution that retails for $3200, but the high bidder had bid over $5000.  Long live capitalism and free enterprise.||||reg||6
